course: dictionary
lesson: 3115
title: What is an election?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An election is when people vote to choose someone, such as a leader, a government or a class representative. Everyone gets a say, and the person with the most votes wins. Schools hold elections too, for example to choose the school council.
explain: «They disagree honestly, and the next election lets everyone choose again.» People can disagree, and the vote is still fair. When the next election comes, everyone gets to choose again.
explain: Before an election, candidates try to get noticed, the way a new cereal does. «Adverts, catchy slogans, posters, signs on lawns and big cheering rallies» are all ways to persuade people to vote for them.
fact: «Election» means a time when people vote to choose someone.
fact: A candidate is a person who wants to be chosen in an election.
fact: Useful phrases: general election, hold an election, win an election, election day.
fact: A political party writes a manifesto, a plan of promises, and then tries to win elections to carry it out.
fact: In maths, votes are counted and shown in bar charts, and the winner is the one with the most votes.
exercise: «Schools hold elections for school council.» What is an election? | When a class lines up in a row | When the bell rings for lunch | When a pupil writes a story for the class | *When people vote to choose someone
exercise: «Before an election, candidates try to get noticed with posters and catchy slogans.» What is a candidate? | *A person who wants to be chosen in an election | A person who sells cereal | A person who counts the votes | A type of bar chart
exercise: In a class election, how do you know who the winner is? | *Whoever has the most votes | Whoever has the longest name | Whoever shouts the loudest | Whoever sits at the front
test: Which phrase means to be chosen because you got the most votes? | To count the bars on a chart | To hold an election | *To win an election | To write a manifesto
test: «News reports in 2025 said the UK government planned to lower the voting age to 16 for general elections.» What is a general election? | A poster on someone's lawn | *A national vote to choose the government | A game played in class | A vote about what to have for lunch
exam: «A political party writes a manifesto of promises, then tries to win elections to carry it out.» What is a manifesto? | A list of cereal adverts | A loud shout at a rally | *A plan of promises a party writes before an election | A bar chart of votes
